+# Open Bathy Workflows (script-based)
+
+This repository is a **script-first** workflow for generating bathymetry products from:
+
+- **SDB (Satellite‑Derived Bathymetry)** from Sentinel‑2 + optional ICESat‑2 + optional external XYZ soundings
+- **River bathymetry** inferred from a river network + a bank DEM via cross‑section sampling/interpolation
+- **Fusion** of SDB + river products into a single depth raster
+
+## Main entrypoint
+
+Run the full workflow via **`bathy_main.py`**:
+
+```bash
+python bathy_main.py \
+  --aoi="-74.52/-74.23/40.23/40.52" \
+  --start 2024-01-01 \
+  --end 2026-01-01 \
+  --out-dir output/nyc \
+  --extra-xyz-cudem=hydronos,ehydro
+```
+
+`bathy_main.py` orchestrates three sub-pipelines:
+
+1. **SDB** (subprocess call to `sdb_main.py`)
+2. **River** (subprocess calls to `xs_builder.py` then `xs_infer_bathy_raster.py`)
+3. **Fusion** (Python import/call of `fusion.py`)
+
+## Script map
+
+These are the scripts that are *in the execution path* when you run `bathy_main.py` (directly, or via imports):
+
+### Orchestration / shared utilities
+
+- **`bathy_main.py`** — top-level driver; validates config, runs SDB + river, then fuses outputs.
+- **`validation.py`** — pipeline configuration validation.
+- **`checkpoints.py`** — checkpoint bookkeeping so long runs can resume.
+- **`logging_config.py`** — consistent logging setup.
+- **`utils.py`** — common helpers (I/O, CRS helpers, etc.).
+
+### SDB pipeline
+
+- **`sdb_main.py`** — SDB driver; acquires Sentinel‑2 scenes, builds optical features, samples training points from ATL/XYZ, trains a model, predicts rasters.
+- **`s2_optics.py`** — Sentinel‑2 processing (scene search/filter, composites, masks, feature stacks).
+- **`atl.py`** — ICESat‑2 utilities (reading/filters, refraction correction support, track sampling).
+- **`train.py` / `sdb_train.py`** — training dataset construction and model training.
+- **`predict.py` / `sdb_predict.py`** — applying the trained model to create SDB depth rasters.
+- **`align.py`** — alignment/offset handling between sources.
+- **`masks.py`** — land/water/clear-water and related masking logic.
+- **`glint.py`** — (optional) sunglint utilities when enabled.
+
+### River pipeline
+
+- **`river_network.py`** — fetches/builds the river network layers used for cross-sections.
+- **`xs_builder.py`** — builds cross-sections from the river network + DEM.
+- **`xs_infer_bathy_raster.py`** — infers river depths/bed elevations from cross-sections + DEM + optional soundings.
+- **`river_cache.py`** — caching for river intermediates/outputs.
+
+### Fusion
+
+- **`fusion.py`** — combines SDB + river products into the final raster(s) in `out-dir/combined/`.
+
+> Notes
+> - The exact set of modules imported at runtime may vary by options (e.g., enabling/disabling glint correction or choosing different ICESat-2 sources).
+> - The scripts above are the *core path* used by the `bathy_main.py` workflow.
+
+## Archive
+
+Scripts that are not referenced by the current `bathy_main.py` workflow (and were cluttering the root) were moved to:
+
+- **`archive/likely_unused/`**
+
+These are preserved for reference, experimentation, or future reintegration. If you rely on any of them directly, you can either:
+
+- run them from their archived location, or
+- move them back to the repo root and update imports accordingly.
